     "result_text_tail": "ales instead of 25%, with a $4M cash envelope.\n2. Fix the Korean-only labels and take the Amazon listings in-house before scaling.\n3. Raise the awareness threshold for adding retail from 15% to 20%, and start with a store test instead of 600 stores.\n4. Weight the off-Amazon marketing budget toward social media.\n\nThe deck also sets out the five decisions for the March board, review points with a stop trigger, and what evidence would change the recommendation.\n\n**Choices I made without you:**\n- **$40M ambition:** I read \"on the way to $40M by 2030\" as needing a credible path to $40M, not $40M in 2030. The deck proposes $25\u201330M in 2030 and $40M around 2031\u201332, and asks the board to confirm that reading.\n- **Model rules:** inventory is held at four months of product, freight and duty costs. Store counts are treated as in place for the full year, and one-time costs are expensed in the year they occur. There is no tax, discounting or currency effect. Japan has no inventory cost because the pack gives none.\n\n**One limitation:** the sandbox blocked every way of rendering PowerPoint (Chrome, Quick Look, no LibreOffice). I drew the charts as plain PowerPoint shapes and checked layout with my own preview renderer, which found no text overflow. Please page through it in PowerPoint before it goes to the board.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `Onsoo_US_entry_board_deck.pptx`\n- `onsoo_us_entry_model.py` \u2013 reproduces every number in the deck\n- `README.md` \u2013 the answer and the choices above"
